cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Deliberate Line: Taking a Goodhart"
message: "If you use or cite this work, the citation below is offered — but the work is public domain (CC0) and asks nothing of you."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Davidson
    given-names: Noah
abstract: >-
  A sourced, reproducible account of what moves the US stock market over the
  long run: a single ~8%/yr log-linear trend the S&P 500 has held for 56 years,
  a reliable reversion when price runs above it, and a ~2%/yr wedge by which the
  market outruns the economy — read as a deliberate line preserved by a single
  seat rather than an emergent market property. Built entirely from public data
  (FRED, Yahoo Finance) with the reproduction code included and the corrected
  wrong turns left in.
keywords:
  - stock market
  - S&P 500
  - log-linear trend
  - mean reversion
  - Goodhart's law
  - inequality
  - reproducible research
license: CC0-1.0
date-released: 2026-10-14
version: "1.0.0"
